.TH DSHOT 1 "September 2026" "Doubleshot 0.1.0"
.SH NAME
dshot \- caffeinate for closed lids
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dshot
[\-dimsu] [\-t seconds] [\-w pid] [\-\-] [command [args...]]
.br
.B dshot
install | uninstall | status | doctor
.SH DESCRIPTION
Doubleshot holds a closed-lid sleep override for the duration of a command or
terminal session. Concurrent sessions compose. A privileged service restores
normal sleep after the last client ends or crashes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-d
Prevent display sleep while the lid is open.
.TP
.B \-i
Prevent idle sleep. Default when no assertion flags are given.
.TP
.B \-m
Prevent disk idle sleep.
.TP
.B \-s
Create caffeinate's AC system-sleep assertion. The additional closed-lid hold
applies on both AC and battery.
.TP
.B \-u
Declare user activity. With no timeout, Apple's assertion defaults to five seconds.
.TP
.BI \-t " seconds"
End after this duration. Zero means no deadline. Ignored when a command is given.
.TP
.BI \-w " pid"
End when this process exits. Ignored when a command is given.
.SH TERMINAL LIFETIME
Terminal closure releases the hold. In tmux, detaching preserves the pane and
its hold; closing the pane ends it. A run without a controlling terminal follows
the client/workload lifetime. Wrapped commands keep their exit code and input/output.
.SH DISPLAY
Lid closure removes display-awake assertions and requests display sleep,
including connected external displays. The current session is locked
and lock state is checked. Reopening re-creates assertions, including user activity.
.SH INSTALLATION
The first run installs the helper with administrator authentication. After a CLI upgrade,
run dshot install to update the protected service. Run dshot uninstall before removing
the CLI.
.SH RECOVERY
Socket disconnect releases a lease. Otherwise five-second heartbeats maintain a
twenty-second lease. launchd restarts the service; an independent reaper handles
stalled writers. These are nominal timing values, conditional on a functioning OS.
A preexisting unowned SleepDisabled setting is not adopted or reset.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Wrapped command status is preserved. Administrative or service failures return 1;
invalid arguments return 2. Signals use status 128 plus the signal number.
.SH SEE ALSO
caffeinate(8), pmset(1), launchd(8)
